  "text": "This sentence wastes space. The phrase science is fun appears three times. Instead of writing every repeat, a compressor can store a phrase once. Later repeats become short references to that earlier phrase. The remaining symbols are then translated into bits. Common symbols can use shorter bit patterns than rare ones. To open the file, the reader follows the references and rebuilds every original character. Nothing is guessed, nothing is lost. But already compressed data may barely shrink. Zip saves space only when it finds useful structure. Compression is not deleting information, it is writing the same information more efficiently.",
